"""Caxton: Autonomous path-scoped long-form text transformation and audit engine.

Caxton is specialized for large-scale text reasoning across whole repositories:
auditing documentation drift, harmonizing style and terminology across
multi-document corpuses, resolving cross-file contradictions, restructuring
large specifications, and synchronizing documentation against codebases.

Unlike iterative coding tools that operate in tight compile/test loops, Caxton
defaults to aggressive bulk inlining (up to 1 MB) to provide the model with a
comprehensive global overview of an entire text or documentation tree at once.
Codebases may be provided as read-only reference (--read) to audit documentation
drift, but Caxton's mutations (--edit) are tailored for prose, specs, and
documentation.
"""

# Tests: skills/agent-tools/tests/test-caxton

